[1mThe bug:[22m The C code uses a namespace macro [38;5;10m#define SPX_NAMESPACE(s) SPX_##s[0m (defined in [38;5;10mparams.h[0m) to prefix all exported symbols with [38;5;10mSPX_[0m. The test runner (via [38;5;10mcando2[0m) loads the shared library and looks up the symbol [38;5;10mSPX_initialize_hash_function[0m via [38;5;10mdlsym[0m. However, the Rust translation exported the function as [38;5;10minitialize_hash_function[0m — without the [38;5;10mSPX_[0m prefix — causing a [38;5;10mdlsym[0m failure ([38;5;10mundefined symbol: SPX_initialize_hash_function[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe fix:[22m A one-line change in [38;5;10mtranslated_rust/src/lib.rs[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// Before:
pub unsafe extern "C" fn initialize_hash_function(ctx: *mut context::SpxCtx) {

// After:
